# Exercises roles/asmb8_baremetal_install's own logic -- the fan-out guard,
# destructive-confirmation gate, required-variable checks, the forward-looking
# disk-safety guard, and the resumability guard -- entirely on localhost, with
# no network access beyond 127.0.0.1 and no privilege escalation. See
# tasks/main.yml's header comment for exactly what is and is not covered here,
# and why: this role's validate.yml/state.yml phases are pure Ansible logic
# (assert/stat/file/include_vars) that never touch the BMC at all, so they can
# be tested today without any mock server. Its probe/attach_media/arm_boot/
# reset/observe phases talk real IPMI (asmb8_info/asmb8_power/asmb8_boot) and
# real iUSB (asmb8_media), and NEITHER of those has a mock server in this
# collection yet that this target can drive -- tests/integration/mock_servers/
# currently has asp_server.py/iusb_server.py (the iUSB/.asp media plane) but
# nothing at all for the IPMI/RMCP+ plane this role's probe/arm_boot/reset/
# observe depend on. tasks/main.yml's final scenario documents that gap loudly
# rather than silently passing over it.
#
# context/controller because every task this role runs is `delegate_to:
# localhost` (see roles/asmb8_baremetal_install/meta/main.yml), and the nested
# ansible-playbook runs this target drives need the controller's
# ansible-playbook and collection path.
context/controller
skip/windows
